From: AztecBot <tech@aztec-labs.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 21:48:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] test(aztec-nr): make confirmed_to_hinted constrained

noir-lang/noir#13705 scopes the unconstrained-to-constrained fn coercion
exemption to the arguments of an unconstrained callee. `BoundedVec::map`
is constrained, so passing the unconstrained `confirmed_to_hinted` to it
is rejected from Noir v1.0.0-rc.3 on. The helper only copies fields
across, so it does not need to be unconstrained.

diff --git a/noir-projects/aztec-nr/aztec/src/note/note_getter/test.nr b/noir-projects/aztec-nr/aztec/src/note/note_getter/test.nr
index e6e524b4a974716319d8bed3a6dbf5dcb4bc46e9..e8256638ab8166569492b895e18eaf05e330ea6c 100644
--- a/noir-projects/aztec-nr/aztec/src/note/note_getter/test.nr
+++ b/noir-projects/aztec-nr/aztec/src/note/note_getter/test.nr
@@ -44,7 +44,7 @@ where
     assert_eq(count, vec.len());
 }
 
-unconstrained fn confirmed_to_hinted<Note>(confirmed: ConfirmedNote<Note>) -> HintedNote<Note> {
+fn confirmed_to_hinted<Note>(confirmed: ConfirmedNote<Note>) -> HintedNote<Note> {
     HintedNote {
         note: confirmed.note,
         contract_address: confirmed.contract_address,
